{
  "benchmark": "slice5-ai-50",
  "pool_ref": "active-pool-v1",
  "about": "50 fixed AI requests. 'expected' is the hard constraints a careful reader takes from the request (written by hand, not by the parser); the benchmark uses it to check the parser and to compute precision@10 / recall@10. City may be a list when the request names an area. Soft words (quiet, nice, cheap, near the beach) are not hard constraints, so they are not in 'expected'.",
